ting in severe outcomes including death from complications like bloody diarrhea. These findings highlight the narrow therapeutic index of 氟尿嘧啶 and the critical need for metabolic screening prior to administration [Data: Relationships (12718, 12722); Entities (6103, 17097)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"叶酸钙 enhances 氟尿嘧啶’s antitumor efficacy through pharmacokinetic synergy\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The combination of 叶酸钙 and 氟尿嘧啶 represents a well-documented beneficial drug interaction. Pharmacokinetic evidence indicates that elevated intracellular folate levels potentiate the inhibitory effect of 氟尿嘧啶 metabolites on thymidylate synthase, a key enzyme in DNA synthesis. This mechanism translates into improved clinical response rates in colorectal cancer patients receiving the combination versus 氟尿嘧啶 alone. Multiple sources corroborate this finding, reinforcing the standard use of leucovorin (叶酸钙) as a modulator in 5-FU-based regimens [Data: Relationships (40498); Entities (4261, 6103)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"米索硝唑 and other agents can dangerously increase 氟尿嘧啶 toxicity\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Co-administration of 米索硝唑 with 氟尿嘧啶 significantly increases the latter’s toxicity by reducing its clearance, prolonging its half-life, and elevating systemic exposure. This unfavorable interaction exemplifies how certain radiosensitizers or adjunctive therapies can inadvertently exacerbate chemotherapy-related adverse effects. Clinicians must exercise caution when combining such agents, as even preparatory treatments with 米索硝唑 can lead to life-threatening toxicities, including myelosuppression and gastrointestinal damage [Data: Relationships (40501); Entities (7651, 6103)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"氟尿嘧啶 interacts antagonistically with 氟尿嘧啶苷, potentially reducing efficacy\",\n            \"explanation\": \"There is evidence suggesting that 氟尿嘧啶 and 氟尿嘧啶苷 exhibit antagonistic interaction when co-administered, which may compromise therapeutic outcomes. The data notes that concurrent use 'affects efficacy,' implying interference at the metabolic or receptor level. While details are limited, this highlights the importance of avoiding unverified combinations of fluoropyrimidine analogs, as structural similarities do not guarantee synergistic or even additive effects [Data: Relationships (40499); Entities (6103, 6104)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"法华令 shows route-dependent interaction with 氟尿嘧啶\",\n            \"explanation\": \"法华令 (warfarin) interacts with 氟尿嘧啶 only when the latter is administered via continuous infusion, leading to prolonged prothrombin time and increased bleeding risk. Notably, this interaction does not occur with oral 氟尿嘧啶, indicating a route-specific pharmacokinetic phenomenon. This nuance is critical for anticoagulated cancer patients requiring chemotherapy, as switching administration routes could mitigate dangerous coagulopathy [Data: Relationships (40498); Entities (6447, 6103)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"氟尿嘧啶 belongs to the 抗嘧啶类代谢药物 class with characteristic metabolism and toxicity profile\",\n            \"explanation\": \"氟尿嘧啶 is formally classified under 抗嘧啶类代谢药物, a category of antimetabolites that interfere with pyrimidine-dependent DNA/RNA synthesis. Its metabolism occurs primarily in the liver and intestinal mucosa, leading to variable and often incomplete absorption after oral dosing. The primary toxicities—gastrointestinal mucosal injury and bone marrow suppression—are directly tied to its mechanism of action and metabolic pathway. This classification contextualizes its clinical behavior and aligns it with other agents sharing similar risks and monitoring requirements [Data: Relationships (57542); Entities (6103, 10910)].\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"rating\": 7.5,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The community poses a high clinical impact due to 氟尿嘧啶’s narrow the